# Domain differences: original vs replication effect sizes
Data: `data/meta-regression_joined_data_heterogeneity_in_replication_projects.csv` (86 pairs, 60 cols, no dups, no NA in analytic cols).
Script: `analysis/domain_shrinkage.py` (single run, output in `results.txt`). seed=20261022, bootstrap 10k.

Main metric: unweighted paired Fisher-z difference `d = fiso - fisr`. Relative metrics (`rr/ro`, `|rr|/|ro|`) reported in parallel.
Precision-weighted WLS `w = 1/(se_fiso^2+se_fisr^2)` as mandatory sensitivity layer. Note `se_* == 1/sqrt(n-3)` exactly,
so precision weights are pure (harmonic-type) sample-size weights.

